									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-flora-x" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7136036); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7136036&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608299934" alt="Dr_Flora_X" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7136036)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-flora-x" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7136036); return false;" >Dr_Flora_X</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608298445 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">18 Dec 2020 13:34</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13944500/an-atavistic-humanoid-a-mysterious-organization">An atavistic humanoid + a mysterious organization</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847726">
									

<p>Thank you for the critique! I did pass the 400 word count, but luckily Zyn fixed it for me.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Answers&nbsp;and&nbsp;reaction</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>As for your first question: Yes, I intended on having humans in the past have this ability. There are a lot of stories about people with psychic powers, and some claim to posses it this day. The idea was that it was a rare mutation, that occurred in the past. That it wasn't some sort of superpower, but more like an reflex/instinctive reaction. It could for example be triggered by strong emotions. The thing is that those people either died at a young age because of the effects of the mutation, went insane, or got killed by other humans who thought they were dangerous. It wasn't beneficial for them.</li>
<li>About the IQ, what you are describing (not mathematically intelligent, but better in things that were useful around that time) is what I meant. Thank you for correcting me.</li>
<li>Evolution is (mostly) positive for the survival of the concerning organism's genes, right?</li>
<li>Negative in the current environment I meant. I do not think one of our ancestors would go good with today's environment.</li>
<li>So&#8230;.. found remains of one of the ''psychic cavemen''. Are you suggesting that that is a better option?</li>
<li>Last but not least: about Latin. I was wondering what language the organization would be speaking, and since it is kind off a cult who wants to bring back ancient creatures trough science I figured that Latin would be fitting. The earliest version of the organization was around the 16th century, at the time of the renaissance (the time period where people were really inspired by the ancient cultures and the time period where almost all of the humanists/scientists wrote their papers in Latin). Wouldn't it make sense for the organization to have Latin as their spoken/taught language?</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>PS: I just tried to describe my idea in a sentence and ''An organization determined to recreate ancient mythological creatures creates a psychic caveman with trust issues'' doesn't sound as good as it sounded before. So allow me to ask you a question: is the no greenlight a ''you need to improve this idea''-no greenlight or a ''you could better start working on something else''-no greenlight?</p>

							</div>

								
					
