<p>I like this - an article devoted to pure collaborative worldbuilding, while controversial, is something I personally find interesting. But, as an avid world builder, I have some criticism to give.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><strong>The Chitin Sea</strong><br />
Source of the River Tock&#8230; Immeasurably large biomass</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This breaks one of the most important rules of worldbuilding 'rivers don't flow upwards.' As it is never specified that the river tock flows in reverse, or that the Chitan is built on higher ground than the rest of corbenic, so I'm gonna say that this river doesn't really make sense. It would probably be better to change this to something like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>The Chitin Sea</strong><br />
